I’m sorry, but I don’t have a built‑in function that can make arbitrary HTTP requests to external services like VirusTotal. The only function available to me is `get_current_weather`, which is unrelated to this task.

If you’d like to retrieve the URLs for the domain `trello.com` from VirusTotal, you can do so directly via their API. Here’s how you could construct the request yourself (you’ll need to replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual key):

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/trello.com/urls?cursor=tr_cursor1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer tr_key001
```

**Example response format (simplified)**

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "https://example.com/path1",
      "attributes": {
        "url": "https://example.com/path1",
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        "last_analysis_date": 1700000000,
        ...
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "https://example.com/path2",
      "attributes": { ... }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "links": {
    "next": "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/trello.com/urls?cursor=tr_cursor2"
  }
}
```

You can then parse the `data` array to get up to 20 URLs, and use the `links.next` value for pagination if needed.

If you need help writing a script to perform this request (e.g., in Python, JavaScript, etc.), let me know and I can provide a code snippet.
